abstract: >
  The Interdependent Way is an indisciplinary ethical and psychological framework
  grounded in competence-based ethics, Jungian analytical psychology, and the formal
  treatment of symbolic resonance as a functional cognitive operator. The work defines
  interdependency as reciprocal capability rather than mutual vulnerability, and treats
  archetypal and mythic structures as methodological instruments rather than metaphor or belief.
